# This repository is LF-only in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# It is not a style preference. `java.ungram` is rejected by its own parser when a line ends in
# CRLF, `xtask -- codegen --check` compares rendered output against a committed file byte for byte,
# and the corpus and golden fixtures are compared the same way. A Windows checkout under the
# default `core.autocrlf=true` breaks all three, so the working-tree ending is pinned here rather
# than left to whatever each contributor's Git is configured to do.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
